# Copy to .env and fill in. Vite reads these at build time, so
# restart `pnpm dev` after changing them.
#
# Without all three values the portals stay in demo mode: they render
# their built-in sample data and never call the network. That is
# the intended state before a Supabase project exists.
#
# Project Settings -> API in the Supabase dashboard.
# The anon key is safe in the browser; Row Level Security is what
# protects the data. Never put the service_role key here.
#
# Sign-in is Clerk's. The publishable key (pk_test_… / pk_live_…) is
# public by design — it only identifies your Clerk instance. Find it in
# the Clerk dashboard under API keys. The Clerk SECRET key (sk_…) must
# never go in this file or in any VITE_ variable: it belongs only in the
# admin-users function's secrets (see docs/CLERK.md).

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
